    "result_text": "Done. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe specification says **membership level 4 requires more than 365 days of tenure**, and a newly created owner (zero tenure) must never exceed level 3.\n\nI updated `membershipLevel(Owner)` in `src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`:\n\n- The pre-tenure factors are unchanged \u2014 base 1, +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0` \u2014 but they are now explicitly capped at **level 3** (`PRE_TENURE_MAX_LEVEL`).\n- **Level 4 is unlocked only by tenure**: `hasTopLevelTenure(...)` adds 1 when the days between `registrationDate` and today exceed `TENURE_DAYS_FOR_TOP_LEVEL` (365). Owners with no registration date (legacy seed data) have no tenure.\n- Raised `MAX_MEMBERSHIP_LEVEL` from 3 to 4 and rewrote the Javadoc to describe the tenure rule.\n\nBecause `BuildOwner` registers a new owner as of the current day, its tenure is 0, so the maximal pre-tenure owner (email present, no namesakes) lands at level 3 \u2014 exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` asserts. The 3-member-household detail in the spec is descriptive of the scenario, not a level factor (the test comment confirms the pre-tenure factors are just email and no-namesake).",
